/A 1044 0 R
/Alt (The box plot displays time to 50 percentage closure in seconds on the vertical axis, ranging from 0 to 7. The horizontal axis shows two categories: Brands and Touch. For Brands, the box extends from approximately 0.7 seconds to 2.1 seconds, with a median line at 1.5 seconds. Individual data points for Brands are scattered between 0.4 seconds and 6.7 seconds, and a diamond symbol representing the mean is at approximately 1.9 seconds. For Touch, the box is much narrower, extending from approximately 0.4 seconds to 0.7 seconds, with a median line at 0.5 seconds. Individual data points for Touch are clustered between 0.4 seconds and 0.8 seconds, and a diamond symbol for the mean is at approximately 0.6 seconds. A horizontal bracket above the boxes indicates a statistical comparison between Brands and Touch, with a p value of 0.032.)
/K 27
/P 28 0 R
/Pg 14 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
