/A 1049 0 R
/Alt (The scatter plot displays Depolarization Fraction, calculated as the absolute value of peak over P2P, on the vertical axis ranging from 0.25 to 0.70. The horizontal axis represents Spike over Baseline Ratio, ranging from 0 to 6. Four data series are plotted: Trigger Hair Primary as filled circles, Trigger Hair Secondary as open circles, Brands Primary as filled squares, and Brands Secondary as open squares. Large black diamonds indicate group means for Primary spikes. A horizontal dotted line is present at 0.50 on the vertical axis. Two shaded vertical bands indicate mean plus or minus standard deviation ranges for Brands Primary and Trigger Hair Primary Spike over Baseline Ratios. The orange band for Brands Primary is centered around 3.25, and the blue band for Trigger Hair Primary is centered around 3.75. Data points for Trigger Hair Primary are generally clustered between 2.5 and 5.5 on the horizontal axis, and 0.40 to 0.55 on the vertical axis. Trigger Hair Secondary points are more dispersed, ranging from 1.5 to 5.5 horizontally and 0.30 to 0.65 vertically. Brands Primary points are mostly between 2.5 and 5.5 horizontally and 0.45 to 0.65 vertically. Brands Secondary points are widely distributed from 1 to 5 horizontally and 0.30 to 0.55 vertically.)
/K 9
/P 28 0 R
/Pg 15 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
