/Alt (The box plot displays Depolarization Fraction, calculated as the absolute value of peak over P2P, on the vertical axis from 0.3 to 0.8. The horizontal axis shows two main categories: Primary and Secondary. Within Primary, there are two groups: Trigger Hair and Brands. Within Secondary, there are also two groups: Trigger Hair and Brands. Each group is represented by a box plot with individual data points and a diamond symbol indicating the group mean. For Primary, Trigger Hair has a median around 0.5, and Brands has a median around 0.5. For Secondary, Trigger Hair has a median around 0.38, and Brands has a median around 0.47. A horizontal dashed line crosses the plot at 0.5. Statistical comparisons are indicated with p values: Primary Trigger Hair versus Primary Brands shows p equals 0.903 ns. Primary Trigger Hair versus Secondary Trigger Hair shows p equals 0.024 with an asterisk. Secondary Trigger Hair versus Secondary Brands shows p equals 0.765 ns. Primary Brands versus Secondary Brands shows p equals 0.118 ns. A vertical dashed line separates the Primary and Secondary comparisons.)
/K 5
/P 28 0 R
/Pg 16 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
