/Alt (The two-panel waveform graph shows normalized amplitude on the vertical axis from minus 0.6 to 0.6 and time from peak in seconds on the horizontal axis from minus 0.2 to 0.6. Panel A displays primary action potentials. The Trigger Hair waveform, represented by a blue line with a lighter blue confidence interval, rises sharply from minus 0.2 to a peak of 0.5 at 0.0 seconds, then declines sharply to minus 0.4 at 0.2 seconds, and gradually increases to 0.0 at 0.6 seconds. The Brands waveform, represented by an orange line with a lighter orange confidence interval, rises from minus 0.1 to a peak of 0.1 at 0.0 seconds, then declines to minus 0.1 at 0.2 seconds, and gradually increases to 0.1 at 0.6 seconds. The Trigger Hair peak is significantly higher than the Brands peak. Panel B displays secondary action potentials. The Trigger Hair waveform rises from minus 0.2 to a peak of 0.4 at 0.0 seconds, then declines to minus 0.2 at 0.2 seconds, and gradually increases to 0.0 at 0.6 seconds. The Brands waveform rises from minus 0.1 to a peak of 0.1 at 0.0 seconds, then declines to minus 0.1 at 0.2 seconds, and gradually increases to 0.0 at 0.6 seconds. In both panels, the Trigger Hair waveform shows a more pronounced and earlier peak depolarization compared to the Brands waveform.)
/K 27
/P 28 0 R
/Pg 17 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
